      "html": "<aside class=\"ds-inspector\"><small>จุดเสนอ รอสำรวจ</small><h2>จุดกระชัง</h2><span>เครื่องทำงาน</span><dl><div><dt>แหล่งจ่าย</dt><dd>ไฟสำรอง</dd></div><div><dt>กำลังโหลดจำลอง</dt><dd>120 W</dd></div></dl></aside>",
      "css": ".ds-inspector{font-family:\"Manrope Variable\",\"IBM Plex Sans Thai\",sans-serif;width:274px;max-width:100%;padding:18px;background:#FFFFFFF7;border-radius:22px;box-shadow:0 8px 26px #1F2D5A14;color:var(--pg-navy,#1F2D5A)}.ds-inspector small{font-size:10px;color:var(--pg-muted,#657A91)}.ds-inspector h2{font-size:16px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.55;margin:3px 0 14px}.ds-inspector>span{display:inline-flex;border-radius:8px;padding:5px 9px;font-size:11px;background:#E8F8F1;color:#13775F}.ds-inspector dl{margin:14px 0;font-size:12px}.ds-inspector dl>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #E8EFF5}.ds-inspector dt{color:var(--pg-muted,#657A91)}.ds-inspector dd{margin:0;text-align:right;font-weight:500}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The shared community work surface",
    "overview": "The established light iOS-style community interface combines white and sky surfaces, navy Thai text, generous rounded corners and the original ปลากะพงสามน้ำ vector mascot. The exact PowerGuard brand palette remains the authority; technical scenes retain dark spatial controls when detail needs contrast.\n\nThe shared coastal scene lets people select proposed equipment and follow one simulated event through the inspector, charts and incident history. Audience modes change terminology and available actions while retaining the same underlying state. This is a browser-local demonstrator: telemetry, loads, positions, water and weather models remain visibly simulated or proposed.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Short Thai labels and explicit electrical status words.",
      "A shared scene with compact, legible operation surfaces.",
      "Original vector mascot, restrained ambient shadows and local fonts.",
      "Simulation and field-evidence boundaries remain visible."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Status Has Words Rule",
        "body": "Use explicit status words alongside color; distinguish electrical outage, telemetry offline and sensor fault.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Brand Is Exact Rule",
        "body": "Preserve brand.json color values. Use the implemented darker derivatives for readable controls and status text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Shared State Rule",
        "body": "Scene, inspector, charts, timeline and history describe the same simulator state. Audience mode changes presentation and actions.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Depth Supports Operation Rule",
        "body": "Soft shadows separate white operation surfaces from the physical scene; avoid using elevation to imply a measured or installed asset.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the exact brand palette and the Manrope Variable / IBM Plex Sans Thai source fonts.",
      "Do label values, proposed monitoring positions, demonstration loads and geometry according to their evidence.",
      "Do keep the scene selection and equipment inspector synchronized across all three audience modes.",
      "Do preserve a reachable 2D view, reduced motion behavior, opt-in audio and local export paths.",
      "Do retain critical records when a toast is closed or an event is acknowledged."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use physical water color to claim salinity, dissolved oxygen or measured depth.",
      "Don't present local notes as delivered to authorities or the demonstrator as connected hardware.",
      "Don't replace the authentic vector mascot with an invented fish or use the private composition reference as a site asset.",
      "Don't place a transient incident notice over the selected equipment inspector or mascot."
    ]
  }
